    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d558-a1-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0674" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg632"/>

                <head>B.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Flag-Steamer
                                Philadelphia,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Hampton Roads,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 26, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your report of the 14th instant, regarding
                    the seizure of the Golden Eagle, and enclosing some information elicited from
                    her crew, by an examination, has been received.</p>
                <p>There is not, I think, evidence given in your letters and its enclosures,
                    sufficient for the condemnation of the Golden Eagle, and unless you know of
                    additional proof, enough to condemn her, which would justify sending her in for
                    adjudication, it would be well to release her.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. P. LEE, <hi rendition="#italic">A. R. Admiral, Com’dg N. A. B.
                            Squadron.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Lieut. Com. <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. E. DeHaven,</hi> U. S. N., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Com’dg U. S. S. Penobscot, off Wilmington, N.
                            C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
